 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "Why did a sultan destroy his own army?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Because his army had become the empire's biggest problem. In 1826, Mahmud the Second wiped out the Janissaries."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Who were the Janissaries?",
   "scene": "bellini",
   "date": "1400s",
   "place": "Ottoman Empire",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The sultan's elite infantry, founded in the thirteen hundreds. One of the first standing armies in Europe, paid in salaries and armed with guns."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So what went wrong?",
   "scene": "aga",
   "date": "1700s",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.32,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Over time, sons joined their fathers' units, and many members ran shops instead of training."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "By 1826, about a hundred and thirty-five thousand men drew Janissary pay. Many were not real soldiers.",
   "scene": "numbers",
   "date": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "They made and unmade sultans. In 1807 they overthrew Selim the Third, who had tried to build a modern army.",
   "scene": "selim3",
   "date": "1807",
   "place": "Istanbul",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What did the empire look like then?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1826",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Still huge, but shrinking. Russia had taken Crimea, and Greece was in revolt."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So how did Mahmud do it?",
   "scene": "mahmud2",
   "date": "June 1826",
   "place": "Istanbul",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In June 1826, he announced a new, European-style army. Just as he may have planned, the Janissaries revolted."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "This time, loyal troops and cannons were ready. The Janissary barracks were shelled and burned. Thousands died.",
   "scene": "massacre",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.45,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.2
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And what did the Ottomans call it?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The Auspicious Incident. After almost five centuries, the Janissaries were gone."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Mahmud changed even the clothes: soon officials swapped the turban for the fez.",
   "scene": "mahmud",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.3,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.25,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Did the new army work right away?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1830",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Not exactly. It was too new to win the next war with Russia, and in 1830 Greece became independent."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: reform in a rose garden, and the sick man of Europe. Like the video and follow History Sketches."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: the sick man of Europe",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ]
}